  <div id=3D"lesson-content">
    <div class=3D"text-longform" data-controller=3D"richtext"><h2 style=3D"=
text-align:left;"><strong>What is a Design System?</strong></h2><p style=3D=
"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"></p><div class=3D"rich-text--image" =
style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/qRB8gLKx/image-1=
-13.png" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.posti=
mg.cc/qRB8gLKx/image-1-13.png" style=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=3D"=
text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;<br>A design system is essenti=
ally a collection of reusable UI components that work well together to help=
 create more consistent and cohesive user interfaces. If a company has a de=
sign system, designers can use it to build high-fidelity mockups with ease =
and efficiency, thereby saving time and effort in the design process.<br><b=
r></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">What's in a Design System?</h1><p styl=
e=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base">A design system usually includes=
 a style guide, component library and pattern library. These three elements=
 work together to create a comprehensive system for managing designs.&nbsp;=
<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">What is a style guide?</h1><p st=
yle=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"></p><div class=3D"rich-text--i=
mage" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/VsrRxzqf/i=
mage-2-5.png" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.=
postimg.cc/VsrRxzqf/image-2-5.png" style=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=
=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;<br>A style guide is a doc=
ument that outlines the rules for your design. This can include typography,=
 color, and other visual elements. A style guide helps to keep your design =
consistent and easy to use.<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">What =
is a component library?</h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-bas=
e"></p><div class=3D"rich-text--image" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=
=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/qRYz0XxR/image-2-4.png" target=3D"_blank" data-tur=
bo=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/qRYz0XxR/image-2-4.png" style=
=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base=
"> &nbsp;<br>A component library is a collection of all the reusable compon=
ents that make up your design. This can include buttons, forms, and other i=
nterface elements. A component library makes it easy to find and use the ri=
ght element for your design.<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">What=
 is a pattern library?</h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base=
"></p><div class=3D"rich-text--image" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D=
"https://i.postimg.cc/65VdKqyX/image-1-14.png" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=
=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/65VdKqyX/image-1-14.png" style=
=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base=
"> &nbsp;<br>A pattern library is a collection of reusable design patterns.=
 Design patterns are groups of components that designers use to solve usabi=
lity issues=E2=80=93for example, a navbar with a logo, or a contact form. P=
atterns are typically more comprehensive than components, including both vi=
suals and code. Because patterns are comprehensive, they can take more time=
 to create. However, they can save time in the long run by making it easier=
 to create new pages that match the look and feel of the overall site.<br><=
br>A style guide, component library and pattern library work together to cr=
eate a comprehensive system for managing your design. Having all three of t=
hese elements will help to keep your design consistent, easy to use and eas=
y to update.<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">Benefits of having a=
 design system</h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base">There =
are many reasons why every organization should consider implementing a desi=
gn system, including:<br><br>1. It <strong>enhances consistency</strong> in=
 user experiences across touchpoints =E2=80=94 A design system simplifies t=
he prototyping process by providing designers with ready-made UI elements t=
hat they can simply drag and drop into their prototypes. This not only stre=
amlines the designer's workflow but also ensures consistent interactions wi=
thin each prototype (e.g., same button sizes, typefaces, color schemes). By=
 keeping designs aligned with established<br><br>2. Design systems <strong>=
accelerate collaboration</strong> between different teams of designers and =
developers who may be working on separate projects or platforms within an o=
rganization =E2=80=94 this can save precious time spent explaining decision=
s to other team members so everyone can move forward quickly and efficientl=
y.<br><br>3. <strong>Faster time-to-market</strong> for new products and se=
rvices due to increased reuse of pre-existing designs and code. This will n=
ot only help designers maintain a consistent look and feel, but it will als=
o minimize the amount of time needed to train new team members on the organ=
ization's design language and style guidelines.<br><br>4. Design systems al=
so create <strong>more effective prototypes </strong>by reducing the number=
 of details that need to be mocked up in a prototype on an iterative basis =
=E2=80=94 this means less time spent designing new mockups for every single=
 change or modification discovered during usability testing, QA testing, et=
c.&nbsp;<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">Step-by-step guide on ho=
w to build a design system</h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-=
base"></p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"><strong>1. Defi=
ne the core principles of your design system</strong></p><p style=3D"text-a=
lign:left;" class=3D"text-base">These should include things like style guid=
elines, UI patterns and components, color palettes, typography and iconogra=
phy, as well as any other key aspects that are essential to the overall loo=
k and feel of your brand or product.<br></p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" c=
lass=3D"text-base"><strong>2. Gather all of your existing UI components</st=
rong></p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base">Gather all of yo=
ur existing UI components into a centralized library so that you have a sin=
gle source of truth for all of your reusable UI elements. This will make it=
 easier for designers to find and use these existing components when buildi=
ng prototypes or designing new features or products.<br></p><p style=3D"tex=
t-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"><strong>3. Develop an iterative workflow=
 process</strong></p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base">Deve=
lop an iterative workflow process for creating new parts and pieces within =
your design system as needed. This might involve working with developers to=
 create prototypes, sharing and communicating feedback with other designers=
, and testing your designs to ensure that they work as intended.<br></p><p =
style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"><strong>4. Use style guides =
and pattern libraries&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=
=3D"text-base">Use tools like style guides and pattern libraries to documen=
t everything about your design system so that it can be easily accessed and=
 shared with others across the organization. This will help you maintain co=
nsistency in your design language over time and make it easier for new desi=
gners to get up to speed on how things are done within the team or organiza=
tion.<br></p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"><strong>5. S=
et up regular reviews of the design system&nbsp;</strong></p><p style=3D"te=
xt-align:left;" class=3D"text-base">Consider setting up regular reviews of =
the design system to assess whether any changes need to be made based on us=
er feedback or market trends, etc. Maintaining an evolving design system re=
quires continuous iteration and refinement in order to remain effective ove=
r time. By following these steps, you can build a robust and cohesive desig=
n system that can help improve the user experience across all of your produ=
cts and services!<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">Where to host a=
 design system?</h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"></p><=
div class=3D"rich-text--image" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https:=
//i.postimg.cc/9fvQnPPY/SVG.png" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><im=
g src=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/9fvQnPPY/SVG.png" style=3D"width:100%;"></a><=
/div><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;<br>Where to =
host your design system is another key consideration. There are a few diffe=
rent options:<br></p><ul><li><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-ba=
se"><strong>Hosting on a dedicated server</strong>: This option gives you t=
he most control over your design system, but can be expensive and requires =
more maintenance.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=
=3D"text-base"><strong>Hosting on a cloud service</strong>: This option is =
cheaper and easier to set up, but you'll have less control over your design=
 system.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-b=
ase"><strong>Hosting on a version control system</strong>: This option give=
s you more control than hosting on a cloud service, but can be more difficu=
lt to set up and maintain.</p></li></ul><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=
=3D"text-base"><br>We recommend <strong>hosting the Design System in Figma<=
/strong>. Figma is a great option for many reasons:<br><br>- Figma is built=
 for collaboration, making it easy for multiple people to work on the same =
design system at the same time.<br>- It has <strong>extensive versioning an=
d commenting features</strong>, so you can keep track of changes and have d=
iscussions about them all in one place.<br>- Figma's component libraries ma=
ke it <strong>easy to reuse pieces of your design system</strong> across di=
fferent projects.<br><br>There are many YouTube videos that will guide you =
through creating a design system in Figma step-by-step. We recommend watchi=
ng these videos if you want to learn how expert designers build design syst=
ems:<br><br><strong>Build it in Figma: Create a Design System =E2=80=94 Fou=
ndations</strong> (by Figma)<br><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=
=3DEK-pHkc5EL4&amp;t=3D959s%EF%BF%BC%EF%BF%BCCreate" target=3D"_blank" data=
-turbo=3D"false">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DEK-pHkc5EL4&amp;t=3D959s=
</a><br><br><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DEK-pHkc5EL4&amp;t=
=3D959s%EF%BF%BC%EF%BF%BCCreate" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><st=
rong>Create</strong></a><strong> a Design System with Figma - Full Course</=
strong> (by freeCodeCamp)<br><a href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DR=
YDiDpW2VkM%EF%BF%BC%EF%BF%BC%EF%BF%BCOverall" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=
=3D"false">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DRYDiDpW2VkM</a><br><br><br><a =
href=3D"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DRYDiDpW2VkM%EF%BF%BC%EF%BF%BC%EF%=
BF%BCOverall" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false">Overall</a>, there is =
no "right or wrong" place to create a design system; it will often depend o=
n factors like cost, accessibility, and internal requirements. Ultimately, =
the key is simply to find a solution that works best for your organization.=
<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;">Do you need a design system?</h1=
><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"><br>Most companies, espe=
cially the ones that offer digital products or services, already have a des=
ign system in place. That's why it's very likely you'll be working with one=
 if you choose to be an in-house designer.&nbsp;<br>If you want to be a fre=
elancer, you don't need a design system of your own as every project is dif=
ferent and will need a different set of UI elements and components. On top =
of that, creating a design system is very time-consuming so it could take s=
everal months just to build it.&nbsp;<br><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:le=
ft;">Great Design Systems examples:</h1><h2 style=3D"text-align:left;"><a h=
ref=3D"https://m3.material.io/" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><str=
ong>Google Material Design System</strong></a></h2><p style=3D"text-align:l=
eft;" class=3D"text-base"></p><div class=3D"rich-text--image" style=3D"text=
-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/cL09fPVQ/unnamed-1-1.png" tar=
get=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/cL09fP=
VQ/unnamed-1-1.png" style=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=3D"text-align:=
left;" class=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;<br>Google's publicly shared Material Des=
ign system is based on the principle that good design should be consistent,=
 understandable, and accessible. The system includes a library of reusable =
components, a set of principles for designing user interfaces, and a set of=
 tools for creating and managing design assets.</p><p style=3D"text-align:l=
eft;" class=3D"text-base"><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D=
"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/guidelines/o=
verview/" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false">Apple Human Interface Guid=
elines</a></h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"></p><div c=
lass=3D"rich-text--image" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://i.p=
ostimg.cc/m236nb4c/apple-design-resources-2x.jpg" target=3D"_blank" data-tu=
rbo=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/m236nb4c/apple-design-resour=
ces-2x.jpg" style=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=3D"text-align:left;" c=
lass=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;</p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-b=
ase">The Apple Human Interface Guidelines are a set of principles that gove=
rn the design of Apple products. They are based on the belief that simplici=
ty is the key to a great user experience. As such, their design philosophy =
stresses the need for clear and easy-to-use interfaces. The guidelines also=
 emphasize the importance of user feedback, stating that " feedback should =
be immediate, understandable, and actionable." In addition to these core pr=
inciples, the guidelines also include detailed information on Apple's desig=
n system features. These include Auto Layout, which helps developers create=
 responsive interfaces that adapt to different screen sizes; Core Animation=
, which makes it easy to create sophisticated animations and transitions; a=
nd iCloud, which allows users to seamlessly sync their data across multiple=
 devices. By adhering to these guidelines, developers can create apps that =
provide a superior user experience.</p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=
=3D"text-base"><br></p><h1 style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://at=
lassian.design/" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false">Atlassian Design Sy=
stem</a></h1><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"></p><div cla=
ss=3D"rich-text--image" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://i.pos=
timg.cc/yNjQ8nx7/meta.png" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><img src=
=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/yNjQ8nx7/meta.png" style=3D"width:100%;"></a></div=
><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;<br>Atlassian's D=
esign System is a set of tools and guidelines that help developers create c=
onsistent, user-friendly interfaces. The system includes a library of reusa=
ble components, a color palette, and a set of icons. It also provides guida=
nce on typography, layout, and accessibility. The system is based on Atlass=
ian's design philosophy, which places a focus on simplicity, usability, and=
 collaboration. The company believes that by making the design process more=
 efficient and consistent, they can help developers create better products.=
 The Design System has been designed to work with Atlassian's products, but=
 it can also be used to create interfaces for other web-based applications.=
</p><p style=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"><br><br></p><h1 style=
=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://polaris.shopify.com/" target=3D"_b=
lank" data-turbo=3D"false">Shopify Design System - Polaris</a></h1><p style=
=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"></p><div class=3D"rich-text--imag=
e" style=3D"text-align:left;"><a href=3D"https://i.postimg.cc/NFd2y9T9/imag=
e-1-15.png" target=3D"_blank" data-turbo=3D"false"><img src=3D"https://i.po=
stimg.cc/NFd2y9T9/image-1-15.png" style=3D"width:100%;"></a></div><p style=
=3D"text-align:left;" class=3D"text-base"> &nbsp;<br>The Shopify Design Sys=
tem is a set of guidelines and tools that help teams design and build consi=
stent, high-quality products. The system is built around three core princip=
les: flexibility, scale, and quality. These principles guide everything fro=
m the way Shopify designs its products to the way it builds its design syst=
em.<br><br>The Shopify Design System includes a wide range of features, all=
 of which are designed to help teams work more efficiently and effectively.=
 For example, the system includes a comprehensive set of UI components that=
 can be easily customized to meet the needs of any project. In addition, th=
e system provides an extensive color palette and typographic style guide th=
at helps ensure consistency across products. Finally, the Shopify Design Sy=
stem includes a toolkit of resources that makes it easy for teams to get st=
arted with designing and building consistent, high-quality products.<br></p=
></div>
  </div>

